.TH XIL\-SFX\-CSV "1" "2026\-07\-02" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-sfx\-csv \- flatten sfx_<TAG>.json configs to CSV, one row per effect
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-sfx\-csv
[\-h] [\fI\,PATH\/\fR] [\-\-output FILE] [\-\-json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads one or more
.B sfx_<TAG>.json
configuration files and writes a flat CSV (or JSON array) with one row per
effect.  Columns include the effect key, prompt, type, duration, loop flag,
and source path.
.PP
When
.I PATH
is omitted, scans
.B configs/\fR\fI<slug>\fR/
under the current workspace root for all sfx_*.json files matching the active
show.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATH
Path to a specific sfx_*.json file or a configs directory (default: workspace configs/<slug>/)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write CSV output to FILE (default: stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output a JSON array to stdout \(em no banner, safe to pipe to jq
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Export all SFX configs for the active show:
.B xil sfx\-csv
.TP
Export a specific episode's SFX config:
.B xil sfx\-csv configs/the413/sfx_the413_S01E01.json \-\-output sfx_review.csv
.TP
Pipe to jq for filtering:
.B xil sfx\-csv \-\-json | jq '.[] | select(.type == "ambience")'
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xil (1),
.BR xil\-parse (1),
.BR xil\-produce (1),
.BR xil\-parsed\-csv (1)
.SH AUTHOR
John Brissette <xilcmd@gmail.com>
